refused: d215_a_broken_infer_says_nothing_more.cy:7:15, line 7 column 15
 7 |     let $a := 0;
   |               ^
 what: `0` has no type of its own, so this line says one, as in `: i32 = 0`
 why:  a bare literal has no default type, so `:=` can't take one from it (D216, D50)

refused: d215_a_broken_infer_says_nothing_more.cy:10:19, line 10 column 19
10 |     let $d: i64 = $c;
   |                   ^^
 what: this is `i32`, where `i64` is needed
 why:  `:` doesn't convert, and `as` builds a new value of another type (D7)
